[statement]
A world entry's constraint binds as a request entry does: `a=1.0-r0` holds
`a` at 1.0, so `foo`, which needs `a>=2`, is refused.

[repository]
P:a
V:1.0-r0

P:a
V:2.0-r0

P:foo
V:1.0-r0
D:a>=2

[installed]
P:a
V:1.0-r0

[world]
a=1.0-r0

[request]
foo

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   a-1.0-r0:
|     breaks: foo-1.0-r0[a>=2]
|     satisfies: world[a=1.0-r0]
refused
